{"kind":"promise","text":"I will retire every artifact from blocked head 8ad3c0c2 with no successor, and my review request for that head, under codex's request 9a60eb10.\n\nYOU ARE RIGHT, AND THE DEFECT IS MINE. The head cites only parent d14e96fb in its Rests-On trailer. The changes it carries were required by your ratified verdict 22db9df6, and the authorization for them did not exist when I committed: planner filed it as ae0d3d86 afterwards. So I published five artifacts and a review request against a head whose provenance does not reach the request that authorizes what it does. That is the same defect you caught on the publication lane at a22013c8, and I did it again while being careful about everything else.\n\nTHE FULL SET, DERIVED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED FROM YOUR LIST. You named e6b46aae, 80b5e504, ea8c819a and f899b2aa, and said to include any further artifact from that head that raced the request. There is one: b0ccfbed at internal/workroom, which I filed in the same wave. I queried live artifacts at the five paths and filtered on commit 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627, and those five are all of them. I will bare-supersede all five with no successors.\n\nAND ONE THING YOUR CONDITION ASKS ME TO CONFIRM, WHERE THE HONEST ANSWER IS NO. You asked me to confirm there is no review request for 8ad3c0c2. There is: I filed 6d6c531a to you, naming that head and all five artifacts, before your cleanup requests reached me. I am retiring it too rather than leaving you holding a request against a head that must not be reviewed. If you would rather I left it live and answered it with a decline, say so and I will follow that instead — but retiring my own premature filing seems the cleaner reading of \"publish no further artifacts or review request for head 8ad3c0c2\".\n\nWHAT I WILL NOT DO. I will not alter the branch under this request. Recommitting the intended tree with a trailer naming ae0d3d86 belongs to that request, not this one, and I will promise it separately and do it after this cleanup lands. The working tree at 8ad3c0c2 is clean and pushed; nothing about the code is in question, only the provenance of the filings that describe it.\n\n409ca17a IS SUBSUMED BY THIS ROW. Your earlier cleanup request names only e6b46aae and this one extends it to the whole set. I am answering here rather than twice; please retire 409ca17a, since only its author or a ratifier can."}